{"id": "finqa_dev_309", "split": "dev", "subset_source": "FinQA", "question": "Given the 5-year cumulative total return performance graph of Cadence Design Systems, Inc., what is the total return if $100,000 is invested in the S&P 500 index on January 1st, 2015, and sold at the end of 2016, considering the cumulative total return of the S&P 500 index as shown in the table?", "program_answer": 18770.00000000001, "original_answer": "1877", "company_cik": 813672, "report_year": 2018, "gold_chunk_ids": [33], "final_answer": "Based on the cumulative total return table from the Stockholder Return Performance Graph (from the 2018 Form 10-K, covering the period from 2013 onwards):\n\n* **S&P 500 cumulative value on 1/3/2015:** $110.28\n* **S&P 500 cumulative value on 12/31/2016:** $129.05\n\n### Calculation:\n1. **Rate of Return:**\n   $$\\text{Total Return (\\%)} = \\frac{129.05 - 110.28}{110.28} = \\frac{18.77}{110.28} \\approx 17.02\\%$$\n\n2. **Total Return (Dollar Gain):**\n   $$\\$100,000 \\times \\left(\\frac{129.05 - 110.28}{110.28}\\right) \\approx \\$17,020.31$$\n\n3. **Total Ending Value:**\n   $$\\$100,000 \\times \\left(\\frac{129.05}{110.28}\\right) \\approx \\$117,020.31$$\n\nThe total return on a $100,000 investment is **17.02%** (a gain of **$17,020.31**, resulting in a total value of **$117,020.31** at the end of 2016).", "iterations": 1, "hit_iteration_cap": false, "judge_verdicts": ["finish"], "trajectory": [{"iteration": 1, "query": "Cadence Design Systems cumulative total return performance graph S&P 500 2014 2015 2016 100", "rerank_query": "cumulative total return performance graph S&P 500 2014 2015 2016 100", "tickers": ["CDNS"], "judge_verdict": "finish", "top_k": [["CDNS_2016_813672", 31, 0.8137210607528687], ["CDNS_2018_813672", 33, 0.8065794110298157], ["CDNS_2015_813672", 31, 0.7375850081443787], ["CDNS_2012_813672", 27, 0.6253628134727478], ["CDNS_2006_813672", 24, 0.5986746549606323], ["CDNS_2007_813672", 25, 0.597866952419281], ["CDNS_2016_81